.TH STUDIOGTK 1 "October 2026" "vst-ace" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
studiogtk \- the session window in GTK: a tab per plug\-in, beside the tracker
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B studiogtk
.RI [ \-\-synth " plug\-in" "]... [" \-\-tracker "] [" \-\-song " file.trk] [" \-\-quit\-after " ms]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B studiogtk
is the vst\-ace session window in GTK, the counterpart of
.BR studio (1):
it opens on a blank canvas; File > New synth opens a tab hosting one plug\-in
\(em the full dwstudio host, with its programs, parameters, keyboard, patch
banks and editor \(em and File > New tracker opens the pattern sequencer in a
tab of its own. Only the tab in front answers the computer keyboard, and the
tabs mix into one audio stream, so several plug\-ins play at once.
.PP
Plug\-ins built for Windows, macOS and Linux all load as native code; there is
no Wine and no emulation. They are hosted out of process by default, so one
that faults costs a helper rather than the session.
.PP
The tracker tab is the same tracker the standalone binary runs, one per
process. A track's destination list offers the synth tabs beside it as
"this window: <name>", and picking one plays the track into the tab directly,
in process, with sample\-accurate timing \(em no trip through the ALSA
sequencer. A tab closing unregisters itself first, so tracks routed there
fall back to the windows their songs name.
.SH OPTIONS
A session can be named rather than clicked together. Each
.B \-\-synth
opens a synth tab with that plug\-in loaded,
.B \-\-tracker
opens the tracker tab, and
.B \-\-song
loads a song into it, opening the tab first if needed.
.B \-\-route
plays the numbered track into the first synth tab, in process, and starts the
song \(em the scripted proof of the direct routing.
.B \-\-smoke
runs the scripted exercise for that many milliseconds, printing each tab's
callback count and peak once a second, then quits;
.B \-\-quit\-after
just quits then. With no arguments the window opens on the blank canvas.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GDK_BACKEND
Editors embed through an X11 window id, so this wants to be \fBx11\fR under
Wayland; XWayland is enough. Override it for a native Wayland window and no
native editors.
.TP
.B GSK_RENDERER
Forced to \fBcairo\fR: GTK's GL renderer on the toplevel's window hierarchy
breaks the GLX contexts native plug\-in editors draw with. Set it yourself to
override.
.TP
.B PEHOST_ISOLATE
Set to 0 to host in process rather than behind the helper.
.TP
.BR DW_PERIOD ", " DW_LATENCY ", " DW_BACKEND
Audio block size (frames), buffer depth (ms) and backend
.RB ( auto ", " pipewire " or " alsa ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR va (1),
.BR studio (1),
.BR dwstudio (1),
.BR pestudio (1),
.BR peload (1).
